  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promote supplementary feeding- Sustainable Production of Supplementary Feeds in Uganda (Supple-F Production)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to adopt a holistic approach to the beef value chain in Uganda, constructed around three main pillars: Specific to the implementation of this call for proposal, shall support small scale operators, especially women and youth, to participate in commercial production of silage, hay making, feedlots management through climate smart practices and in a sustainable manner. Based on the information of beef market requirements especially the quality parameters, the correct combinations of pastures, silage, industrial by products and practises of feed lot management, will be agreed through evidence based analysis by the research institutions, best practises from the Netherlands will be sought, this information will be kept and where necessary updated and becomes the guide for production processes for the supplementary feed</narrative>
  </description>
